IMPORT `date-compat`

§ `Day & Date Definitions and Helpers`

-- Library with some basic functions to enable math with dates and days following ISO 8601
-- Functions return datestamps (Number of days since 1st January 0000).
-- A week begins on Monday
-- Check the test/daydate.l4 file to see examples


§§ `Constants`


@nlg the number of months in a year
`Months in a year`      MEANS 12
@nlg the average number of days in a Gregorian year
`Days in a year`        MEANS 365.2425   -- Considering 4 year leap-cycle with 100 and 400 year exceptions
@nlg the average number of days in a Gregorian month
`Days in a month`       MEANS 30.436875  -- Average month
@nlg the number of days in a week
`Days in a week`        MEANS 7

@nlg the day-of-week number for Monday
`Monday`     AKA `Mon`  MEANS 1
@nlg the day-of-week number for Tuesday
`Tuesday`    AKA `Tue`  MEANS 2
@nlg the day-of-week number for Wednesday
`Wednesday`  AKA `Wed`  MEANS 3
@nlg the day-of-week number for Thursday
`Thursday`   AKA `Thu`  MEANS 4
@nlg the day-of-week number for Friday
`Friday`     AKA `Fri`  MEANS 5
@nlg the day-of-week number for Saturday
`Saturday`   AKA `Sat`  MEANS 6
@nlg the day-of-week number for Sunday
`Sunday`     AKA `Sun`  MEANS 0

@nlg the month number for January
`January`    AKA `Jan`  MEANS 1
@nlg the month number for February
`February`   AKA `Feb`  MEANS 2
@nlg the month number for March
`March`      AKA `Mar`  MEANS 3
@nlg the month number for April
`April`      AKA `Apr`  MEANS 4
@nlg the month number for May
`May`                   MEANS 5
@nlg the month number for June
`June`       AKA `Jun`  MEANS 6
@nlg the month number for July
`July`       AKA `Jul`  MEANS 7
@nlg the month number for August
`August`     AKA `Aug`  MEANS 8
@nlg the month number for September
`September`  AKA `Sep`  MEANS 9
@nlg the month number for October
`October`    AKA `Oct`  MEANS 10
@nlg the month number for November
`November`   AKA `Nov`  MEANS 11
@nlg the month number for December
`December`   AKA `Dec`  MEANS 12



§§ `Type`


§§ `Date Constructors`


GIVEN day   IS A NUMBER
      month IS A NUMBER
      year  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg the date %day%/%month%/%year%
`Date` AKA `Days to date` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_SERIAL (jan1serial PLUS monthDays PLUS day MINUS 1)
    WHERE
        jan1serial MEANS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 year)
        monthDays MEANS `Months since year start to days` month year

GIVEN days  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg the date numbered %days%
`Date` AKA `Days to date` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_SERIAL days

GIVEN date  IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg %date%
`Date` AKA `Days to date` MEANS date

-- Date str  -> parse date string (YYYY-MM-DD, etc.), ignores time/timezone if present
GIVEN str IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
@nlg the date in %str%, if it can be read
`Date` AKA `Days to date` MEANS
    CONSIDER DATEVALUE str
    WHEN RIGHT d THEN JUST d
    WHEN LEFT err THEN
        CONSIDER TODATETIME str
        WHEN JUST dt THEN JUST (DATETIME_DATE dt)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- Date dt  -> extract date from DATETIME (ignores time and timezone)
GIVEN dt IS A DATETIME
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg the date of %dt% in its own time zone
`Date` AKA `Days to date` MEANS DATETIME_DATE dt

-- YMD year month day  -> the date, with its parts in ISO 8601 order.
-- Where `Date` rolls a month or a day that does not exist forward, YMD
-- refuses, and its reason says whether the month or the day is wrong.
-- The year must be a whole number and is not otherwise checked.
-- `Year month day` is another name for YMD.
GIVEN year  IS A NUMBER
      month IS A NUMBER
      day   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg the date %year%-%month%-%day%, if there is one
`YMD` AKA `Year month day` MEANS
    IF      month AT LEAST 1
        AND month AT MOST 12
        AND FLOOR month EQUALS month
    THEN IF      DATE_YEAR  candidate EQUALS year
             AND DATE_MONTH candidate EQUALS month
             AND DATE_DAY   candidate EQUALS day
         THEN candidate
         ELSE REFUSE "YMD: that month has no such day in that year"
    ELSE REFUSE "YMD: the month is not a whole number from 1 to 12"
    WHERE
        candidate MEANS Date day month year



§§ `Datestamp Constructors`


GIVEN date  IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the day number of %date%
`Day` AKA `Date to days` MEANS
    DATE_SERIAL date

GIVEN day   IS A NUMBER
      month IS A NUMBER
      year  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the day %day%/%month%/%year%
`Day` AKA `Date to days` MEANS
    DATE_SERIAL (Date day month year)

GIVEN days  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the day numbered %days%
`Day` AKA `Date to days` MEANS
    days

GIVEN year  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg the first day of %year%
`Year` MEANS
    Month 1 year

GIVEN date  IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg the first day of the year containing %date%
`Year` MEANS
    Year (DATE_YEAR date)

GIVEN month IS A NUMBER
      year  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg the first day of month %month% of %year%
`Month` MEANS
    Date (Day 1 month year)
            
GIVEN days  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg the first day of the month containing the day numbered %days%
`Month` MEANS
    Month (Date days)

GIVEN date  IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg the first day of the month containing %date%
`Month` MEANS
    Month (DATE_MONTH date) (DATE_YEAR date)

GIVEN week  IS A NUMBER
      year  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg the Monday of ISO week %week% of %year%
`Week` MEANS
    Year year
        PLUS (3 MINUS `Days in a week`) MINUS o
            PLUS (w TIMES `Days in a week`)
    WHERE
        w MEANS FLOOR week
        o MEANS (`Days in a week` PLUS 2
            PLUS (`Weekday of 1st day of year` year))
                MODULO `Days in a week`

GIVEN days  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg the Monday of the ISO week containing the day numbered %days%
`Week` MEANS
    IF   w EQUALS 0
    THEN Date (days MINUS (`Days in a week` MINUS 1))
    ELSE Date (days MINUS w PLUS 1)
    WHERE
        w MEANS `Weekday of` days

GIVEN date  IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg the Monday of the ISO week containing %date%
`Week` MEANS
    Week (Day date)



§§ `Month Helpers`
-- Convenience functions for months so you can write: January 1 1972

GIVEN day   IS A NUMBER
      year  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg %day% January %year%
`January` AKA `Jan` MEANS
    Date day 1 year

GIVEN day   IS A NUMBER
      year  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg %day% February %year%
`February` AKA `Feb` MEANS
    Date day 2 year

GIVEN day   IS A NUMBER
      year  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg %day% March %year%
`March` AKA `Mar` MEANS
    Date day 3 year

GIVEN day   IS A NUMBER
      year  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg %day% April %year%
`April` AKA `Apr` MEANS
    Date day 4 year

GIVEN day   IS A NUMBER
      year  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg %day% May %year%
`May` MEANS
    Date day 5 year

GIVEN day   IS A NUMBER
      year  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg %day% June %year%
`June` AKA `Jun` MEANS
    Date day 6 year

GIVEN day   IS A NUMBER
      year  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg %day% July %year%
`July` AKA `Jul` MEANS
    Date day 7 year

GIVEN day   IS A NUMBER
      year  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg %day% August %year%
`August` AKA `Aug` MEANS
    Date day 8 year

GIVEN day   IS A NUMBER
      year  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg %day% September %year%
`September` AKA `Sep` MEANS
    Date day 9 year

GIVEN day   IS A NUMBER
      year  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg %day% October %year%
`October` AKA `Oct` MEANS
    Date day 10 year

GIVEN day   IS A NUMBER
      year  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg %day% November %year%
`November` AKA `Nov` MEANS
    Date day 11 year

GIVEN day   IS A NUMBER
      year  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg %day% December %year%
`December` AKA `Dec` MEANS
    Date day 12 year


GIVEN days  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the month number of the day numbered %days%
`Month of the year` MEANS 
    `Month of the year` (Date days)

GIVEN date  IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the month number of %date%
`Month of the year` MEANS                     -- Returns the number of the week of this date
    `Month of days` 1 (`Months since year start to days` (DATE_MONTH date PLUS 1) (DATE_YEAR date))
    WHERE
        GIVEN i IS A NUMBER
              c IS A NUMBER
        `Month of days` MEANS
            IF    i LESS THAN `Months in a year` AND a LESS THAN c
            THEN  `Month of days` (i PLUS 1) c
            ELSE  i
            WHERE
                a MEANS `Months since year start to days` (i PLUS 1) (DATE_YEAR date)




§§ `Datestamp Math Helpers`


GIVEN month IS A NUMBER
      year  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the number of days in %year% before month %month%
`Months since year start to days` MEANS
    IF    m LESS THAN 1
    THEN  0
    ELSE  `Days in month` m year
              PLUS `Months since year start to days` m year -- Recursively add all days of months that year
    WHERE
        m MEANS FLOOR month MINUS 1

GIVEN days  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the number of days of the year before the month containing the day numbered %days%
`Months since year start to days` MEANS
    `Months since year start to days` (Date days)

GIVEN date  IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the number of days of the year before the month containing %date%
`Months since year start to days` MEANS
    `Months since year start to days` (DATE_MONTH date) (DATE_YEAR date)

GIVEN month IS A NUMBER
      year  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the number of days in month %month% of %year%
`Days in month` MEANS
    IF       m EQUALS 4   -- April
          OR m EQUALS 6   -- June
          OR m EQUALS 9   -- September
          OR m EQUALS 11  -- November
    THEN  30
    ELSE  IF    m EQUALS 2
          THEN  IF    `is leap year` y
                THEN  29
                ELSE  28
          ELSE  31
    WHERE
        m MEANS 1 PLUS (FLOOR month MINUS 1)
                    MINUS (FLOOR ((month MINUS 1)
                        DIVIDED BY `Months in a year`))
                            TIMES `Months in a year`
        y MEANS FLOOR year
                    PLUS FLOOR (month DIVIDED BY `Months in a year`)

GIVEN days  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the number of days in the month containing the day numbered %days%
`Days in month` MEANS
    `Days in month` (Date days)

GIVEN date  IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the number of days in the month containing %date%
`Days in month` MEANS
    `Days in month` (DATE_MONTH date) (DATE_YEAR date)

GIVEN year  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the number of days in %year%
`Days in year` MEANS
    IF   `is leap year` year
    THEN 366
    ELSE 365

GIVEN date  IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the number of days in the year containing %date%
`Days in year` MEANS
    `Days in year` (DATE_YEAR date)

GIVEN year  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the day number of 1 January of %year%
`Years to days` MEANS
    (year TIMES 365)
        PLUS  FLOOR (y DIVIDED BY 4)   -- consider leap years
        MINUS FLOOR (y DIVIDED BY 100)
        PLUS  FLOOR (y DIVIDED BY 400)
    WHERE
        y MEANS FLOOR (year MINUS 1)

GIVEN date  IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the day number of 1 January of the year containing %date%
`Years to days` MEANS
    `Years to days` (DATE_YEAR date)



§§ `Calendar Arithmetic`


-- Add a whole number of months or years to a date, CLAMPING the day to the last
-- day of the target month when the original day does not exist there. 31 January
-- plus one month is 29 February in a leap year and 28 February otherwise; the
-- first anniversary of 29 February 2024 is 28 February 2025.
--
-- The clamp is not one convention picked from several. It is what Excel's EDATE
-- does, and what `actus-schedule` already did for schedule generation.
--
-- Contrast `Date d m y`, which is LENIENT and ROLLS FORWARD: `Date 29 2 2025` is
-- 1 March 2025, not 28 February. Rolling is right for component arithmetic of the
-- `Date 1 (month PLUS 6) year` kind and wrong for an anniversary, and the two
-- differ by exactly one day on precisely the dates anybody litigates.

GIVEN date   IS A DATE
      months IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg the date %months% months after %date% (capped at the last day of that month)
`add months` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY clampedDay newMonth newYear
    WHERE
        totalMonths MEANS DATE_MONTH date PLUS FLOOR months
        newYear     MEANS DATE_YEAR date
                              PLUS FLOOR ((totalMonths MINUS 1) DIVIDED BY `Months in a year`)
        newMonth    MEANS ((totalMonths MINUS 1) MODULO `Months in a year`) PLUS 1
        lastDay     MEANS `Days in month` newMonth newYear
        clampedDay  MEANS IF   DATE_DAY date GREATER THAN lastDay
                          THEN lastDay
                          ELSE DATE_DAY date

GIVEN date  IS A DATE
      years IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg the date %years% years after %date% (capped at the last day of that month)
`add years` MEANS
    `add months` date (FLOOR years TIMES `Months in a year`)



§§ `Weekday Functions`


GIVEN days  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the day-of-week number (Sunday being 0) of the day numbered %days%
`Weekday of` MEANS
    days MODULO `Days in a week`

GIVEN date  IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the day-of-week number (Sunday being 0) of %date%
`Weekday of` MEANS
    `Weekday of` (Day date)

GIVEN month  IS A NUMBER
      year   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the day-of-week number of the first day of month %month% of %year%
`Weekday of 1st day of month` MEANS
    `Weekday of`
        (Day 1 month year)

GIVEN days   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the day-of-week number of the first day of the month containing the day numbered %days%
`Weekday of 1st day of month` MEANS
    `Weekday of 1st day of month` (Date days)

GIVEN date   IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the day-of-week number of the first day of the month containing %date%
`Weekday of 1st day of month` MEANS
    `Weekday of 1st day of month` (DATE_MONTH date) (DATE_YEAR date)

GIVEN year  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the day-of-week number of the first day of %year%
`Weekday of 1st day of year` MEANS
    `Weekday of` (Year year)

GIVEN date  IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the day-of-week number of the first day of the year containing %date%
`Weekday of 1st day of year` MEANS
    `Weekday of 1st day of year` (DATE_YEAR date)



§§ `Week Functions`


GIVEN days  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the ISO week number of the day numbered %days%
`Week of the year` MEANS 
    `Week of the year` (Date days)

GIVEN date  IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the ISO week number of %date%
`Week of the year` MEANS                     -- Returns the number of the week of this date
    IF    n EQUALS 53 AND `Weeks in year` (DATE_YEAR date) EQUALS 52
    THEN  1
    ELSE  IF    n EQUALS 0
          THEN  `Weeks in year` (DATE_YEAR date MINUS 1)
          ELSE  n
    WHERE
        s MEANS (`Months since year start to days` date)
            PLUS (DATE_DAY date MINUS 1)
        w MEANS (`Days in a week` PLUS 2 PLUS (`Weekday of 1st day of year` (DATE_YEAR date)))
            MODULO `Days in a week`
        n MEANS CEILING ((s PLUS w MINUS 2) DIVIDED BY `Days in a week`)

GIVEN year  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the number of ISO weeks in %year%
`Weeks in year` MEANS             -- Calculating the weeks in a given year using Zeller's Congruence
    IF        h EQUALS 5
          OR (h EQUALS 4 AND `is leap year` year)
    THEN  53
    ELSE  52
    WHERE
        y MEANS FLOOR year MINUS 1
        k MEANS y MODULO 100
        j MEANS FLOOR (y DIVIDED BY 100)
        h MEANS (37 PLUS k
                    PLUS FLOOR (k DIVIDED BY 4)
                    PLUS FLOOR (j DIVIDED BY 4)
                    PLUS (5 TIMES j))
                MODULO `Days in a week`

GIVEN date   IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the number of ISO weeks in the year containing %date%
`Weeks in year` MEANS
    `Weeks in year` (DATE_YEAR date)   




§§ `Attribute Checkers`


GIVEN days  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg the day numbered %days% falls on a weekend
`is weekend` MEANS
        w EQUALS Saturday
    OR  w EQUALS Sunday
    WHERE
        d MEANS FLOOR days
        w MEANS `Weekday of` d

GIVEN date  IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %date% falls on a weekend
`is weekend` MEANS
    `is weekend` (Day date)


GIVEN days  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg the day numbered %days% falls on a weekday
`is weekday` MEANS
    NOT `is weekend` days

GIVEN date  IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %date% falls on a weekday
`is weekday` MEANS
    `is weekday` (Day date)

GIVEN year  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %year% is a leap year
`is leap year` MEANS
            y MODULO 4   EQUALS 0
    AND NOT y MODULO 100 EQUALS 0
    OR      y MODULO 400 EQUALS 0
    WHERE
      y MEANS FLOOR year

GIVEN date   IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %date% falls in a leap year
`is leap year` MEANS
    `is leap year` (DATE_YEAR date)




§§ `Relative time phrases`


GIVEN day   IS A NUMBER
      date  IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg day %day% of the period beginning on %date%
`on day` MEANS
    date PLUS day MINUS 1

GIVEN date   IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg the day after %date%
`the day after` MEANS
    date PLUS 1

GIVEN date   IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg the day before %date%
`the day before` MEANS
    date MINUS 1

GIVEN date   IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg the Monday of the ISO week after the one containing %date%
`the week after` MEANS
    IF    d GREATER THAN `Days in a week`
    THEN  Date (days PLUS d MINUS `Days in a week`)
    ELSE  Date (days PLUS d)
    WHERE
        days MEANS Day date
        d MEANS `Days in a week` MINUS (`Weekday of` days) PLUS Monday

GIVEN date   IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg the Monday of the ISO week before the one containing %date%
`the week before` MEANS
    `the week after` date MINUS (`Days in a week` TIMES 2)

GIVEN date   IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg the first day of the month after the one containing %date%
`the month after` MEANS
    Date 1 (DATE_MONTH date PLUS 1) (DATE_YEAR date)

GIVEN date   IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg the first day of the month before the one containing %date%
`the month before` MEANS
    IF    DATE_MONTH date EQUALS 1
    THEN  Date 1 12 (DATE_YEAR date MINUS 1)
    ELSE  Date 1 (DATE_MONTH date MINUS 1) (DATE_YEAR date)

GIVEN date   IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg the first day of the year after the one containing %date%
`the year after` MEANS
    Date 1 1 (DATE_YEAR date PLUS 1)

GIVEN date   IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg the first day of the year before the one containing %date%
`the year before` MEANS
    Date 1 1 (DATE_YEAR date MINUS 1)


§§ `Comperators`

GIVEN date1  IS A DATE
      date2  IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg the earlier of %date1% and %date2%
`the earlier of` MEANS
    IF   date1 AT MOST date2
    THEN date1
    ELSE date2

GIVEN date1  IS A DATE
      date2  IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg the later of %date1% and %date2%
`the later of` MEANS
    IF   date1 GREATER THAN date2
    THEN date1
    ELSE date2


§§ `Stringify for months and weekdays`


GIVEN date  IS A DATE 
GIVETH A STRING
@nlg the name of the month containing %date%
`Name of month` MEANS
    `Name of month` (Day date)

GIVEN days  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A STRING
@nlg the name of month %days%, or of the month containing that day number if not 1 to 12
`Name of month` MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 0 THEN "January" ELSE
        IF m EQUALS 1 THEN "February" ELSE
            IF m EQUALS 2 THEN "March" ELSE
                IF m EQUALS 3 THEN "April" ELSE
                    IF m EQUALS 4 THEN "May" ELSE
                        IF m EQUALS 5 THEN "June" ELSE
                            IF m EQUALS 6 THEN "July" ELSE
                                IF m EQUALS 7 THEN "August" ELSE
                                    IF m EQUALS 8 THEN "September" ELSE
                                        IF m EQUALS 9 THEN "October" ELSE
                                            IF m EQUALS 10 THEN "November" ELSE
                                                "December"
    WHERE
        d MEANS FLOOR days
        m MEANS IF    d GREATER THAN 0 AND d LESS THAN 13
                THEN  d MINUS 1
                ELSE  FLOOR (DATE_MONTH (Date d) MINUS 1)

GIVEN days   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A STRING
@nlg the day-of-week name of the day numbered %days%
`Name of weekday` MEANS
    IF w EQUALS Monday THEN "Monday" ELSE
        IF w EQUALS Tuesday THEN "Tuesday" ELSE
            IF w EQUALS Wednesday THEN "Wednesday" ELSE
                IF w EQUALS Thursday THEN "Thursday" ELSE
                    IF w EQUALS Friday THEN "Friday" ELSE
                        IF w EQUALS Saturday THEN "Saturday" ELSE
                            "Sunday"
    WHERE
        w MEANS `Weekday of` days

GIVEN date   IS A DATE
GIVETH A STRING
@nlg the day-of-week name of %date%
`Name of weekday` MEANS
    `Name of weekday` (Day date)



§§ `Native overloads`

GIVEN a IS A DATE
      b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %a% is on or after %b%
`__GEQ__` MEANS
    Day a AT LEAST Day b

GIVEN a IS A DATE
      b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %a% is on or before %b%
`__LEQ__` MEANS
    Day a AT MOST Day b

GIVEN a IS A DATE
      b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %a% is after %b%
`__GT__` MEANS
    Day a GREATER THAN Day b

GIVEN a IS A DATE
      b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %a% is before %b%
`__LT__` MEANS
    Day a LESS THAN Day b

GIVEN a IS A DATE
      b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %a% is before %b%
a `is before` b MEANS a LESS THAN b

GIVEN a IS A DATE
      b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %a% is after %b%
a `is after` b MEANS a GREATER THAN b

GIVEN a IS A DATE
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg the date %b% days after %a%
`__PLUS__` MEANS
    Date (Day a PLUS b)

GIVEN a IS A DATE
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg the date %b% days before %a%
`__MINUS__` MEANS
    Date (Day a MINUS b)

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg the date %a% days after %b%
`__PLUS__` MEANS
    Date (a PLUS Day b)

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
@nlg the date numbered %a% less the day number of %b%
`__MINUS__` MEANS
    Date (a MINUS Day b)

GIVEN a IS A DATE
      b IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the sum of the day numbers of %a% and %b%
`__PLUS__` MEANS
    Day a PLUS Day b

GIVEN a IS A DATE
      b IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the number of days from %b% to %a%
`__MINUS__` MEANS
    Day a MINUS Day b
